{
  "schema": 15,
  "id": "battery-power-v1",
  "name": "9 V power: battery only",
  "version": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 0
  },
  "description": "How a battery-only pedal (no DC jack) takes its 9 V. The battery's + is V+; its - goes to the IN_ring port: wire it to the guitar input's ring (set IN's jack to stereo), so the pedal is on only with a guitar cable plugged in, which is why battery pedals say to unplug them when not in use. Then the 9 V input filter to V+F (its values from the ProCo Rat, ElectroSmash). The battery's form sets how drained it is. The same ports as the DC jack and battery block, so either can replace the other.",
  "tags": [
    "power",
    "battery",
    "filter"
  ],
  "template": true,
